@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed — Quality trade-off hypotheses and non-negotiable invariants
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Current authorization / synchronized invalidation" as A
rectangle "Latency / dependency pressure" as L
rectangle "Exact immutable history / protected references" as H
rectangle "Storage / cleanup / recovery burden" as S
rectangle "More worker concurrency" as C
rectangle "Queue delay / web resource contention" as W
rectangle "AFTER MVP: untrusted-code containment" as I
rectangle "Capacity / setup / operating effort" as O
A --> L : correctness benefit; possible cost to measure
H --> S : integrity benefit; retention/lifecycle cost to assess
C --> W : may reduce waiting while increasing contention
I --> O : required safety boundary; actual resource cost to establish
A -[hidden]down-> H
H -[hidden]down-> C
C -[hidden]down-> I
note bottom of H
 These are hypotheses, not measured correlations or scores.
 Security/history invariants are constraints, not tradeable benchmark points.
 No numerical worker, retention or latency setting is selected.
end note

@enduml
